ation"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/902"} "Arena Carioca 2, Parque Olímpico da Barra, Barra da Tijuca, Rio de Janeiro"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/354505"} "34 from 34 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Another surprise gold medal winner was " [:a {:href "/athletes/134624"} "Fabio Basile"] " in the men’s 66 kg class. He was ranked 29th on the IJF list, and his best result prior to the Olympics was a bronze medal at the 2016 European Championships. On his way to the Rio final, he defeated three opponents by Ippon (full point), including second ranked " [:a {:href "/athletes/123518"} "Davaadorjiin Tömörkhüleg"] " from Mongolia, the 2014 Asian Games gold medalist. He also beat Slovenia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/135876"} "Adrian Gomboc"] ". The Slovenian was the only opponent lower than Basile in the ranking list and in the semi-final he resisted Basile for the complete five minutes but lost by two Shidos (penalties) for non-combativity. In the final Basile faced the top ranked reigning World Champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/134967"} "An Ba-Ul"] " of Korea. Basile surprised him with a Seoi-otoshi (back-drop) scoring an Ippon just 1:24 min into the bout."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Bronze medals went to " [:a {:href "/athletes/112811"} "Rishod Sobirov"] " of Uzbekistan and " [:a {:href "/athletes/120787"} "Masashi Ebinuma"] " of Japan, both previous World Champions. Both were defeated by An in the quarter-finals and semi-finals respectively of the elimination round."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/134624"} "Fabio Basile"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [